    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet amidst the stunning landscape of Aghadoe, Barleymount West presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a detached four-bedroom bungalow enjoying an elevated position and spectacular panoramic views across the Lakes of Killarney and the surrounding mountain scenery.\n\nOccupying a generous site of approximately 0.51 acre, this charming property enjoys a peaceful countryside setting while remaining within easy reach of Killarney town and all the amenities the town has to offer. Its elevated position and southerly aspect combine to create an exceptionally bright and scenic home, with the ever-changing views providing a magnificent backdrop throughout the seasons.\n\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 106 sq. m. and is centred around a spacious living room and kitchen, both of which take full advantage of the property's wonderful outlook. The living room features an open fireplace, while the kitchen incorporates fitted units, a solid-fuel stove and excellent views across the lakes and mountains.\n\nThe property provides four bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom. A number of the bedrooms also benefit from the outstanding views, allowing the scenery to become an integral part of everyday life.\n\nExternally, the property is approached through its own private grounds and benefits from a detached steel-framed shed, offering useful additional storage.\n\nAghadoe is synonymous with some of the finest scenery in the Killarney area. The property is situated in an elevated rural setting approximately 9km from Killarney town, offering the ideal balance between peaceful country living and accessibility.\n\nThe surrounding area is renowned for its spectacular views across Lough Leane, the Lakes of Killarney and the MacGillycuddy's Reeks. Nearby Aghadoe is itself one of Killarney's celebrated viewpoints, looking across Lough Leane towards Ross Castle, Innisfallen Island and the mountains beyond.\n\nThe location also provides easy access to the recreational amenities for which Killarney is internationally renowned. Killarney National Park offers an outstanding choice of walking, cycling and outdoor pursuits, while Ross Castle and Ross Island provide some of the area's most popular lakeside walks and attractions.\n\nFor those who enjoy golf, walking, cycling, fishing and exploring the great outdoors, the surrounding area provides an exceptional natural playground. \n\nWhile the property is perfectly capable of serving as a comfortable family home, it also offers considerable potential for a purchaser wishing to modernise and personalise a property in an exceptional location.\n\nThe combination of its elevated site, southerly aspect, generous grounds, four-bedroom accommodation and panoramic views creates a particularly attractive proposition for those seeking a home where location and outlook are of paramount importance."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 3.13m x 1.97m\nCarpeted hallway\n\nLiving Room - 7.22m x 4.25m\nCarpeted, open fireplace, lake and mountain views\n\nKitchen - 7.2m x 3.07m\nLinoleum flooring to kitchen area, fitted kitchen units, carpeted living area, solid burning stove, lake and mountain views\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.41m x 4.25m\nCarpeted, fitted wardroes\n\nEn Suite - 1.49m x 1.57m\nWC, WHB, shower\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.8m x 2.79m\nCarpeted, fitted wardrobes, lake and mountain views\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.37m x 2.7m\nCarpeted, fitted wardrobes\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.66m x 2.45m\nCarpeted, fitted wardrobes, lake and mountain views\n\nBathroom - 3.38m x 2.28m\nCarpeted, WC, WHB, Bath, partly tiled walls\n\n"
      },
      {
